{"case_id":"T5025","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","stateful_api_protocol","input_semantics","configuration"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["ares_process_fds","ares_process_fds_nolock","ares_process_fd","ares_process","process_read","process_write","ares_event_thread_process_fd"],"reason":"H0 only fuzzes DNS query creation and parsing/writing; it never initializes an ares_channel_t, creates live connection/socket state, or invokes the new event-processing API. The supplied change introduces a fuzz-worthy stateful interface whose behavior depends on event-array contents, nevents consistency, per-FD READ/WRITE masks, duplicate or unknown descriptors, and ARES_PROCESS_FLAG_SKIP_NON_FD. The compatibility wrapper ares_process_fd is especially implicated because its write branch assigns events[nevents - 1].fd = read_fd, so write-only and distinct-read/write combinations require direct coverage.","evidence":["test/ares-test-fuzz-name.c calls only ares_create_query with fixed C_IN, T_AAAA, id 1234, flags 0, and max_udp_size 1024.","test/ares-test-fuzz.c feeds bytes to ares_dns_parse and, after successful parsing, exercises record getters and ares_dns_write; its USE_LEGACY_PARSERS branch only calls ares_parse_*_reply functions.","No H0 path calls ares_process_fds, ares_process_fd, ares_process, process_read, process_write, or configures ares_channel_t connection state.","include/ares.h exposes ares_process_fds(channel, events, nevents, flags), with events optionally NULL only when nevents is 0, event bits ARES_FD_EVENT_READ and ARES_FD_EVENT_WRITE, and ARES_PROCESS_FLAG_SKIP_NON_FD.","ares_process_fds_nolock iterates the same event array separately for reads and writes, ignores ARES_SOCKET_BAD, looks descriptors up through process_read/process_write, and conditionally runs ares_check_cleanup_conns and process_timeouts based on flags.","ares_process_fd constructs up to two ares_fd_events_t entries, merges equal descriptors, and in the write branch visibly stores read_fd rather than write_fd.","ares_event_thread_process_fd maps ARES_EVENT_FLAG_READ/WRITE into the new mask and calls ares_process_fds with ARES_PROCESS_FLAG_SKIP_NON_FD, while the event loop separately calls it with NULL, 0, and ARES_PROCESS_FLAG_NONE."],"recommended_action":"Add a stateful harness that initializes an ares_channel_t with controlled socket/connection I/O and decodes fuzz input into event arrays, nevents, masks, descriptor relationships, and process flags. Exercise ares_process_fds plus ares_process_fd with read-only, write-only, combined, distinct, duplicate, unknown, and ARES_SOCKET_BAD descriptors; include NULL/zero versus inconsistent NULL/nonzero arrays, SKIP_NON_FD versus NONE, repeated calls, timeout/cleanup transitions, and readable data or disconnect/error outcomes."}
